---
title: Russian Lamb Pilaf (Plov)
description: This Russian recipe for lamb rice pilaf features plumped dried prunes and raisins and a healthy pinch of saffron to give it a sunny yellow color.
cuisine: Eastern European
cook time: 1 hour 30 minutes
time required: 1 hour 50 minutes
course: Dinner, Entree, Lunch
prep time: 20 minutes
servings: 6
author: Barbara Rolek
tags: Rice
source: https://www.thespruceeats.com/russian-lamb-pilaf-plov-recipe-1137309
---

Place @raisins{2%ounces} and @prunes{4%ounces} into a #small bowl{} and pour over enough water to cover.
Add @lemon juice{1%tbsp} and let soak for at least ~{60%minutes}. 
Drain. Roughly chop the prunes.

Meanwhile, heat @butter{1%oz} in a #large pan{}.
Add @onion{1}(chopped) and cook for ~{5%minutes}.
Add @lamb{1%lb}(boneless, trimmed, cut into 1/2" cubes), @ground lamb{8%ounces}, and @garlic{2%cloves}(crushed).
Fry for ~{5%minutes}, stirring constantly until browned.

Pour @lamb stock{2/3%cup} into the pan.
Bring to a boil, then lower the heat, cover, and simmer for ~{60%minutes}, or until the lamb is tender.

Add the remaining stock and bring to a boil.
Add @rice{2%cups}(long-grain white, rinsed and drained) and a large pinch of @saffron{}.
Stir, then cover, and simmer for ~{15%minutes}, or until the rice is tender.

Add the drained @raisins{} and drained chopped @prunes{}, and @salt{} and @pepper{} to taste.
Heat through for a few minutes, then turn out onto a warmed #serving dish{} and garnish with sprigs of @parsley{}(flat-leaf).

